edits_description = "The people and stalls were cut out to be used in a composition."
blurb = "Like the rest of the series, this print depicts famous theatrical characters comically reimagined at a market.

Goza (ござ) refers to woven rush mats. While tatami mats were thick and permanent fixtures in homes, goza were often used as the top layer of tatami or as portable, rollable seating for picnics, travelers, and vendors. The mat shop is in the top right of the image."
